---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="P4A — Code of conduct">
  <main>
    <div class="container pt-24">

      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <header class="mb-14">
          <h1 class="mb-3 text-5xl text-p4a-ink font-bold">Code of Conduct</h1>
          <p class="text-xl max-w-prose leading-relaxed tracking-wider">
            This Code of Conduct informs our discussions, interactions, and debates. Playbook for America stands for civility and tolerance at all times. 
            We need not always agree, but we must always respect one another and strive to understand perspectives different from our own.
          </p>
        </header>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-p4a-body-text">
          We the people
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4 ml-6">
          Playbook for America is built on the belief that the work of improving our country belongs to all of us. We welcome people with different experiences, priorities, and perspectives, and we ask every member to participate with respect, tolerance, and a shared commitment to constructive civic dialogue.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-p4a-body-text">
          Respect one another
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4 ml-6">
          Treat every member with respect, even during disagreement. Personal attacks, insults, ridicule, and demeaning language have no place in this community.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-p4a-body-text">
          Engage in good faith
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4 ml-6">
          Participate honestly, constructively, and with the intent to contribute. Represent others’ views fairly, avoid deliberate mischaracterization, and seek understanding before judgment.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-p4a-body-text">
          Debate ideas, not people
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4 ml-6">
          Disagreement is welcome when it remains focused on issues, ideas, and solutions. Do not harass, threaten, or belittle others for their beliefs, background, or identity.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-p4a-body-text">
          Practice tolerance
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4 ml-6">
          Members will bring different experiences, priorities, and perspectives. A healthy community requires openness to viewpoints different from our own, even when we strongly disagree.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-p4a-body-text">
          Protect privacy and safety
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4 ml-6">
          Do not share private, personal, or identifying information about others without permission. Content or behavior that intimidates, exposes, or endangers others is not allowed.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-p4a-body-text">
          Help uphold the standard
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4 ml-6">
          Every member shares responsibility for maintaining a respectful and constructive environment. Violations of this Code of Conduct may result in content removal, account restrictions, or removal from the platform.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
